{
 "about": "C16, lane V2: identical batches hashed by the writer before C16 (`legacy`) and by the one after it (`v2`). Shared by the batch-hash writer (sdk/src/tensorquill/data.py, lane V2), the Python reader (sdk/src/tensorquill/data_checks.py, lane V3) and the Rust reader (server/src/detect/data.rs, lane V7). Written by lane V2 only.",
 "kind_rule": "A batch_hash's kind is the text before its first ':'; a hash with no ':' is of the old writer (kind ''). Two hashes are compared only when their kinds are equal; a pair of two kinds is not compared: never a match, never a difference.",
 "writers": {
  "legacy": "16 hex digits: BLAKE2b-64 over each batch's byte length (int64 LE) and bytes, the bytes int64 LE indices or the ids' text joined by NUL. Frozen from data.py at commit 66b52d7.",
  "v2": "'v2:' and 16 hex digits: BLAKE2b-64 over each batch's byte length and bytes, the bytes a tag ('i') and int64 LE indices, or a tag ('t') and each id's type, byte length and bytes. tensorquill.batch_hash(ids) gives it."
 },
 "verdicts": "Per case: `detector` is the one the case is about; `compared` says whether its hashes may be compared; `incident` is null for no incident of that kind, else keys the incident must have with these values. How a reader says 'not compared' (a not_checked entry, a note, nothing) is the reader's: the fixture pins the verdict only. Records are as `load_records(..., all_attempts=True)` gives them; resolve attempts as the detector does.",
